Done. Tetris builds clean (no warnings, clippy clean) with 7 passing unit tests.

**Structure**
- `src/piece.rs` — 7 tetrominoes with 4 rotations each, colors
- `src/board.rs` — 10×20 grid, collision + line clearing
- `src/game.rs` — state, 7-bag randomizer, gravity/rotation/scoring, speed-per-level
- `src/main.rs` — terminal loop, input, ratatui rendering (board, ghost piece, next piece, score/level/lines)

**Run:** `cargo run`

**Controls:** ←/→ move · ↑ rotate · ↓ soft drop · Space hard drop · p pause · r restart (on game over) · q quit

Features: ghost landing preview, 7-bag piece randomizer, soft/hard drop scoring, line-clear scoring (100/300/500/800 × level), level-up every 10 lines with increasing fall speed, pause + game-over overlays.

Note: it's an interactive TUI, so it needs a real terminal to play (I verified logic via the test suite since there's no TTY here).
